  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.big.s1.title": "Change the type in place, fix half the users",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.big.s1.explain": "Appointment.time becomes a LocalDateTime. Storage, the list and reminders are fixed; 17 compile errors remain. No test can run yet.",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.ev.big.s1": "Change the type in place, fix half the users",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.big.s2.title": "Fix the rest, compile errors spread",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.big.s2.explain": "The detail screen, sorting and formatting helpers drag in errors in other files: 40 errors across 12 files. Three hours pass with the app not running.",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.ev.big.s2": "Fix the rest, compile errors spread",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.big.s3.title": "It compiles; run the tests: 3 fail",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.big.s3.explain": "Late in the afternoon it finally compiles. Three tests fail, and any of the 8 changes could be the cause. Out comes the debugger.",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.ev.big.s3": "It compiles; run the tests: 3 fail",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.big.s4.title": "Revert the whole day",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.big.s4.explain": "The fault cannot be found quickly and the release is near: git reset (put the code back to a saved state) to this morning. 5 hours of work thrown away.",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.ev.big.s4": "Revert the whole day",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.small.s1.title": "Add startsAt beside time; storage writes both",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.small.s1.explain": "Two small changes, each running the tests (green) and committing. Nobody reads the new field yet, so nothing breaks.",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.ev.small.s1": "Add startsAt beside time; storage writes both",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.small.s2.title": "Move the list; move reminders: red",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.small.s2.explain": "The list reads startsAt: green, commit. Reminders read startsAt but treat it as UTC (the international standard time; Vietnam is UTC+7), so they are 7 hours off: a test fails. Only one change is suspect; revert that step, 15 minutes lost.",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.ev.small.s2": "Move the list; move reminders: red",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.small.s3.title": "Redo reminders with the time zone; move detail and sorting",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.small.s3.explain": "The redone reminder step uses the clinic's time zone: green. The detail screen and sorting move to startsAt: green, one commit each.",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.ev.small.s3": "Redo reminders with the time zone; move detail and sorting",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.small.s4.title": "Stop reading time, then delete the old field",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.s.small.s4.explain": "When nothing reads time any more, delete it. Every commit is green; the app is releasable at any commit.",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.ev.small.s4": "Stop reading time, then delete the old field",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.co.try": "Follow the strip left to right; each cell is one change, coloured by the test result after it.",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.co.big.s2": "Seemann tells the story of changing a fundamental class in place: a week later the code still did not compile. The rule drawn from it: for a significant change, do not make it in place; make it side by side. To remember it: do not live in the house while knocking out a load-bearing wall; build the new wall beside the old, then remove the old. [[src:book-seemann]]",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.co.big.s3": "Rule of thumb: each refactoring step must be small enough that you will not have to debug. Needing the debugger means the step was too big. [[src:book-craft]]",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.co.big.s4": "Seemann's threshold: if you can go from one consistent state (it compiles, tests green) to the next in under half a day, nothing special is needed; longer, and you need a strangler. [[src:book-seemann]]",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.co.small.s1": "To change a fundamental data structure, build the new one alongside the old, then move each part of the code over gradually, keeping the tests passing throughout. [[src:book-craft]]",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.co.small.s2": "A test failing right after a small step points at exactly what went wrong. Leave yourself an out: put a tag (a label marking one commit) before a chain of refactorings so you can go back. [[src:book-craft]]",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.co.small.s3": "Kent Beck's advice: for each desired change, make the change easy (this may be hard), then make the easy change. [[src:book-seemann]]",
  "track.cleancode.m.refactor.co.small.s4": "The strangler is named after the strangler fig, which grows around its host tree until the old tree is no longer needed. Martin Fowler named the pattern; Seemann finds it useful at almost any scale. [[src:book-seemann]]",
  "track.cleancode.vz.tab.refactor": "Commit strip",
  "track.cleancode.vz.rf.cap": "Each column is one change, in time order. Top row: the tests after that change; bottom row: whether it was committed.",
